From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:56:23 +0200
Subject: riscv: dts: sophgo: put the Milk-V Duo S i2c4 pads at 3.3V

Mainline gives the Duo S i2c4 group power-source = <1800>. VIVO_D0 and
VIVO_D1 are pins 3 and 5 of the 26-pin header, which is 3.3V, and every other
group in their VDDIO_VIVO domain - the i2c1, pwm0, spi3 and uart2 header
overlays - declares 3300.

The pin controller keeps a single power-source per domain, and
cv1800_set_power_cfg() rejects any group that disagrees with the value already
recorded. The whole pin map of that consumer then fails and it never probes,
with nothing in dmesg. So i2c4 as it stands cannot coexist with any of those
overlays: with overlays=uart2, uart2 probes first and takes the domain at 3300,
and VIVO_D0 and VIVO_D1 are left UNCLAIMED in debugfs.

drive-strength-microamp = <4000> is unaffected. sophgo_pinctrl_oc2reg() picks
the first table entry at or above the target, and that is index 0 in both the
1.8V table (7800) and the 3.3V one (5500), so the register value is the same.

The i2c4 overlay already declared 3300 on these pads; it keeps working, and
now just restates the base.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
@@ -145,13 +145,19 @@ &osc {
 };
 
 &pinctrl {
+	/*
+	 * VDDIO_VIVO is 3.3V: these are pins 3 and 5 of the 26-pin header, and the
+	 * header overlays that take other VIVO pads declare 3300. The domain keeps a
+	 * single power-source, so at 1800 this group and those overlays cannot
+	 * coexist - whichever probes second is refused and never probes.
+	 */
 	i2c4_cfg: i2c4-cfg {
 		i2c4-pins {
 			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_VIVO_D1, 7)>,
 				 <PINMUX(PIN_VIVO_D0, 7)>;
 			bias-pull-up;
 			drive-strength-microamp = <4000>;
-			power-source = <1800>;
+			power-source = <3300>;
 		};
 	};
 
